  "hypothesis": "Operator-supplied forced-promotion policy for this deck. Four rules for the TO_ACTIVE/SWITCH contexts only: (1) a Pokemon that can KO the opponent's Active goes first; (2) Teal Mask Ogerpon ex stays Benched unless it can KO, because its Tera clause makes it immune to all attack damage on the Bench and its Teal Dance works from there; (3) Meowth ex is promoted when NOTHING else on the bench can attack -- Tuck Tail deals 60 and returns it plus attached cards to hand, dodging the 2-prize liability and enabling a second Last-Ditch Catch when replayed; (4) Fezandipiti ex is promoted only when an opponent Pokemon sits at or below 100 HP (exactly Cruel Arrow's damage) AND the opponent's Active cannot KO it in reply.",
  "expected_effect": "Forced promotions after a knockout stop defaulting to raw HP ranking and instead follow deck roles: attacker if one is ready, Ogerpon kept in Tera safety, Meowth ex used as a Tuck Tail escape valve when the bench is dead, Fezandipiti ex only as a conditional sniper.",
